  "answer": "A FastAPI application can manage multiple WebSocket clients and disconnected connections by using the `WebSocket` parameter and catching the `WebSocketDisconnect` exception when a connection is closed. When a connection is closed, the `await websocket.receive_text()` will raise a `WebSocketDisconnect` exception, which can be caught and handled like in the example provided in the documentation. The other clients will receive a message indicating that a client has left the chat.\n\n[advanced/websockets-9]",
